# MAJOR PROJECT UPGRADE: LOVEY'S COMPLETE BUSINESS MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (BMS)

Act as an enterprise software architect, principal full-stack engineer, cybersecurity architect, CRM product designer, inventory management specialist and premium SaaS dashboard UX designer.

We are upgrading the existing Lovey's Bakery & Pizza Corners website.

Your task is to build a complete, enterprise-quality, owner-managed ADMIN DASHBOARD that controls the entire business website and its daily operations.

The owner must be able to independently manage practically every business-facing part of the website without requiring the original developer.

This is not a basic admin panel.

Build a comprehensive Business Management System (BMS) with:

- Store management.
- E-commerce management.
- Order management.
- Inventory management.
- Customer Relationship Management (CRM).
- Payment verification.
- Cake customisation management.
- Product management.
- Category management.
- Website content management.
- Homepage management.
- Gallery and media management.
- Promotions.
- Analytics.
- Staff access control.
- Security management.
- Business settings.

IMPORTANT PROJECT RULES:

1. First inspect the existing repository and complete application.
2. Preserve the working website and all existing business functionalities.
3. Continue using the existing Next.js, TypeScript, Supabase and existing payment architecture wherever appropriate.
4. Do not discard existing database records.
5. Create safe migrations for any schema changes.
6. Do not replace real database functionality with mock data.
7. Do not introduce SMS functionality.
8. Do not introduce AI functionality in the deployed website.
9. Do not create a disconnected or merely visual admin dashboard.
10. Every major admin feature must be connected to its actual backend functionality.

